  "scope": "Complete 1 MiB BLAKE3 hashes, after the already-landed buffered-input optimization. First cohort changes the C-compiled update/helper with the native compression object held fixed. Second cohort compares wholly C-compiled hashes. Not a whole-package native performance or proof claim.",
  "decision": "Median paired candidate/baseline ratios improve in all six runs: 0.751,0.865,0.790 with native compression fixed, and 0.787,0.771,0.746 with pure C. Keep the source refactor. High shared-host noise prevents a precise speedup bound; mixed run B's ratio of separate medians regresses despite its paired median improving. All runs and every sample are retained.",
  "change": {
    "source": "stdlib/hash.oak",
    "description": "Replace private blake3_absorb_block(state):State with blake3_absorb_cv(cv,block,counter,flags):[8]u32. The same ordinary-full-block branch updates cv, increments blocks_compressed and clears block_len locally, retaining every other field. Public signatures, compression, flags and boundary/trap conditions are unchanged.",
    "reason": "The old C update copied the whole 1848-byte state to a temporary on every ordinary 64-byte absorption, including the untouched 1728-byte CV stack. Narrowing helper arguments/results removes that copy.",
    "safety": "No raw pointers, unsafe copy primitive, alias assumption, new optimization option or weakened proof gate. The first checked byte write and delayed final-block closure are unchanged."
  },
